    "created_at": "2020-01-05T18:27:24Z",
    "updated_at": "2020-01-05T18:27:24Z",
    "body": "> It would be amazing if we could add basic language support for any language without coding. Maybe something in the config file? Because we'll...i don't know rust.\r\n\r\nSame\r\n\r\nA user configuration for simple modules following some standard API would be great. Something like https://github.com/starship/starship/issues/664#issuecomment-560447671.\r\n\r\nBut it'd also be great to support full custom (Rust I guess) modules similar to those in `starship/src/modules/`. Starship could look for example in `~/.config/starship/modules` / `%HomeDrive%%HomePath%\\.config\\starship\\modules`. Developers could then build complex modules (e.g. dynamic modules, modules with many options, etc) and distribute them easily.",
    "author_association": "NONE",
    "pin": null,
